 ** v2.0.0
 Architecture migration (offline rendering, no remote web API).
   * mermaid.js is now vendored into the package under ./vendor/mermaid.min.js
     (version 12.3.0).  The previous dependency on the mermaid.ink web API
     (which is becoming a paid service) has been removed; diagrams are
     generated entirely on the local machine.
   * A new Node.js renderer (inst/mermaid_js_render.mjs) runs the vendored
     mermaid.js bundle inside a headless Chromium.  Chromium is a C++
     implementation of the V8 JavaScript engine together with the Blink
     DOM/SVG layout engine, so mermaid receives a real DOM and correct text
     measurement (getBBox) and produces accurate diagrams.
   * The Octave functions mermaid_js_save and mermaid_js_imshow now invoke the
     Node renderer instead of the old Python + mermaid.ink code path
     (inst/mermaid_js_save.py has been removed).
   * Runtime requirements (new): Node.js and a Chromium/Chrome browser.  The
     Chromium executable is located automatically, or overridden with the
     CHROMIUM_PATH environment variable.  Node dependencies are installed with
     "npm install" (puppeteer-core).
   * Build/test note: because the JavaScript runtime is the system Chromium/Node
     (C++), the package itself needs no extra compilation step.  On the test
     machine (WSL Fedora 44) Octave 10.3.0 installs and runs the new
     architecture correctly.
